      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_1971668492": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "carolyn.lee@stryker.com",
          "leftPadding": "3",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "carolyn.lee@stryker.com",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Feb 06 2025 18:52:38 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\">Overview</span></h2>\n<p>MEDPOR has been a trusted name in the industry since 1985, with hundreds of thousands of procedures performed, and more than 100 published clinical reports in reconstructive, cranial, oculoplastic, and cosmetic applications.</p>\n<p>Our MEDPOR product line provides you an array of porous polyethylene solutions for your reconstruction and augmentation needs. We understand that bio-compatibility characteristics of implants are paramount to help surgeons achieve positive patient outcomes. The omni-directional pore structure of our polyethylene implants may increase implant&nbsp;acceptance by allowing the patient‘s native tissue to integrate with the implant.<sup>1</sup> In addition to our comprehensive line of stock MEDPOR implants, we offer CT-based&nbsp;patient-specific implants, putting the implant design in your hands.</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\">Proven.</span></span><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"> Adaptable. Comprehensive.</span></span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Jun 13 2025 22:14:21 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "rightPadding": "5",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
